import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 649 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 650 | 2026-10-24 | **Scales: only the frame and the butler from the book; the right hand's thumb in one step; black keys from the group of 2 (her calls 11:22-11:31).** Built on row 649. (1) The folded 'At the piano' steps under five Scales and Key signature lessons are gone (her 'only the frame and the butler'): those lessons keep the book's picture frame and the butler's Remember line, nothing else. (2) White keys, right hand: no stop on the thumb; after the group of 3, one step says 'Then the thumb goes under: a group of 4, fingers 1, 2, 3, 4' (three steps, not four). (3) The butler's lines in her words: right hand 'A group of 3, a group of 4, finger 5 on top. Only F has different groups.', left hand '5 at the bottom, a group of 4, a group of 3. Only B has different groups.', the same pattern from any note 'Start anywhere and keep T T S T T T S: a black key comes in to keep the pattern.' (4) Black keys, right and left hand: the five keys from the group of 2 up (D♭, E♭, G♭, A♭, B♭), each named with both its names (C♯ / D♭ ...); the left hand's 'one shape' line names D♭, E♭, A♭ and B♭. (5) Both hands: its key buttons from C, a half step at a time (C, D♭, D ... B). (6) All twelve keys: white keys C D E F G A B, black keys from the group of 2, both names on the buttons. (7) On the Home, All twelve keys (its fingering table is in every key) covers Both hands: Scales lists one lesson, not two; Both hands stays in the Toolbox. Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/{patch674.py,lbh.jsx}. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
